    "text_delta": "r:** Bringing this up will sound like an unfocused grievance rather than a legitimate professional critique.\n2. **Follow up for feedback—offer a phone call:** People are far more candid verbally than in writing. Send a polite, forward-looking note:\n   > *\"I know the team is busy, but if a brief 10-minute phone call is easier than a written response, I'd welcome any constructive feedback on areas where I can strengthen my profile for future leadership roles.\"*\n3. **Ask the right questions if you get the call:**\n   * Specifically probe the commercial expectations: *\"Was the panel looking for a stronger business development track record or specific client relationships?\"*\n4. **Use it as cultural data:** If this firm operates as an insular \"old boys' club\" that doesn't respect candidates enough to provide post-interview closure, it may not have been an environment where your leadership style would have thrived anyway.\n",
